id: pm-rust-p0no
title: Match unbounded list JSON to PM CLI 2026.10.2
description: "Add an explicit native unbounded-list JSON envelope with default brief projection, full metadata for all-status reads, published lifecycle/order/filter semantics, and golden tests comparing both real CLIs on the same tracker. Preserve the original native list SDK contract."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: conformance,read-parity,rust
created_at: "2026-10-02T18:56:00.427Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-02T19:53:53.919Z"
deadline: "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: pi-glm-rust-parity
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Both unbounded flags are required with --json; Complete parsed JSON matches PM CLI 2026.10.2 golden envelopes for default, all, terminal status, type, ID, combined and empty selections; Ordering is terminal-last then priority ascending then updated_at descending then canonical ASCII ID; Unknown full metadata is preserved and body omitted; Rustdoc, strict Clippy, full tests and 100 percent line function region branch coverage pass without lowered gates; Matrix documents pagination runtime-schema and remaining command gaps"
parent: pm-rust-u4al
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-rust-u4al,parent,"2026-10-02T18:56:00.427Z",pi-glm-rust-parity,"cli:create:dep",asserted
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T18:56:00.427Z",pi-glm-rust-parity,"Plan: test-first golden differential vs real TS CLI 2026.10.2 with fixed Date driver; implement native list mode; keep SDK Workspace::list contract intact."
  "2026-10-02T18:59:38.814Z",pi-glm-rust-parity,"Ollama session limit interrupted implementation after contract research; no source changes yet. Orchestrator will continue the same unbounded-list slice on an allowed fallback provider after checking fresh quota. Item remains open for work, never closed."
  "2026-10-02T19:01:31.028Z",codex-sol,"Orchestrator continuing implementation directly after both GLM providers exhausted quota and Grok OAuth refresh failed; no additional Codex agent authorized under over-forecast policy. Scope: explicit unbounded full JSON list mode; native legacy list API stays stable; deterministic full-envelope golden tests compare published2026.10.2 and Rust on the same temporary tracker."
  "2026-10-02T19:04:49.535Z",codex-sol,"Test-first RED confirmed: eight full golden envelopes recorded from PM CLI2026.10.2; native list differential fails because --json is not recognized. Implement explicit unbounded compatibility mode with default brief projection and full projection for --all/--status all. Actual ordering is terminal-last, priority ascending, updated_at descending, ID tie-breaker."
  "2026-10-02T19:16:11.308Z",codex-sol,"Nine complete golden envelopes now compare the real TS CLI, the native binary and the native SDK on one shared temporary tracker. Added a sub-millisecond timestamp fixture to enforce JavaScript millisecond comparison with lexical ties. Explicit selector refusal, live-clock and closed-output-pipe paths have direct tests. Full aggregate is running through pm test with required PM CLI2026.10.2; coverage threshold remains100 on lines/functions/regions/branches."
  "2026-10-02T19:19:56.329Z",codex-sol,"Verification PASS: pm test pm-rust-p0no --run --match \"just release-check\" --progress ran aggregate successfully with published PM CLI2026.10.2 required. Formatting, all-target all-feature strict Clippy, complete rustdoc, cargo test, nightly llvm-cov and exact100 line/function/region/branch assertion, cargo audit and changelog check all passed. Native CLI and SDK match nine complete published golden envelopes; existing mutation and multi-branch history differential suites pass. Strict tracker health ok=true (guidance/provenance warnings remain). Dependency backlog receipts are included; no merge, publication, release execution or companion writes. Pagination follow-up is pm-rust-ufzy."
  "2026-10-02T19:22:00.125Z",codex-sol,"Parity PR #58 opened: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/58 . Implementation commit2f7babe passed required aggregate on its source content and a post-commit 7-test raw identity audit. Canonical checkout restored to clean main and fast-forwarded; old toolchain branch retained. Fresh PR CI is separate exact-head evidence and is pending. No upstream issues were filed; no merges or releases."
  "2026-10-02T19:45:29.016Z",codex-sol,"PR #58 review remediation: seven distinct findings across 12 cubic threads. Add failing behavioral regressions before SDK all/status refusal, CLI timestamp validation, and differential availability/interpreter fixes. Retain repository backlog audit receipts, append typo correction with pm CLI, clarify pins and docs, run unchanged just release-check, then react/reply/resolve all bot feedback and request fresh reviews. No merge, close, release or publish."
  "2026-10-02T19:48:17.808Z",codex-sol,"Red-first evidence: all_with_explicit_status_fails_closed failed because SDK accepted the conflict; invalid_list_timestamps_fail_closed failed because empty timestamp returned exit 0; golden_checks_survive_missing_published_tools failed because no native/SDK golden assertions ran. A direct run with missing PM_NODE_INTERPRETER and PM_RUST_REQUIRE_PUBLISHED_CLI=1 incorrectly passed before the fix. Fix now validates clocks through the existing shared validator, rejects SDK all/status, and gates only published comparisons with interpreter probing and strict required-tool refusal."
  "2026-10-02T19:52:33.358Z",codex-sol,The first coverage run exposed one uncovered SDK refusal branch in the separately compiled integration-library instance despite the unit regression passing. Moved the red-first all/status regression to the public SDK integration suite against a nonempty tracker so the actual consumer build executes the refusal. No gate or coverage threshold changed.
  "2026-10-02T19:53:53.919Z",codex-sol,"Final local remediation gate PASSED: pm test pm-rust-p0no --run --match \"just release-check\" --progress, using PM_NODE_CLI=/tmp/claude-1000/rust-wt/ts-cli/node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli (2026.10.2). Includes fmt, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, private rustdoc, all tests, exact 100% lines/functions/regions/branches, cargo audit and changelog-check. Focused regressions passed, including public SDK all/status refusal and missing CLI/interpreter golden/required-mode cases. pm health --strict-exit passes integrity/history with four existing guidance/provenance advisories. Linked-test result tracking is disabled by project policy, so this explicit receipt records the result."
